# Home Robot v2 / Emet – Cursor code rules

## Copyright (new files)
- **New** source/tests you add: `# Copyright (c) Chris Paxton 2026` (use the current year).
- **Never** put `Copyright (c) Hello Robot, Inc.` on new files. Leave existing Hello Robot headers alone when editing old files.
- See **`.cursor/rules/copyright.mdc`**.

## Testing (uv)
- **Setup**: Use **uv**. Install deps including dev (pytest, pytest-timeout): `uv sync` (default groups include `dev`, `sim`, `hand_tracker`, `dynamem`, `da3`). Minimal install: `uv sync --no-default-groups`.
- **Canonical run**: From repo root, run **`uv run emet test`** (or just `emet test` — emet re-execs under `uv run` when in project). This uses `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` in pyproject.toml (testpaths = `src/test`).
- **Useful variants**:
  - `uv run emet test -v` — verbose
  - `uv run emet test --no-sim` — skip sim tests (faster; sim tests run by default)
  - `uv run emet test -v src/test/memory/test_memory_backends_smoke.py` — smoke tests for SVM, DynaMem, GraphEQA
  - `uv run emet test -k test_red_cylinder` — only red-cylinder tests
- **Three memory backends**: SVM (instance memory), DynaMem (voxel semantic), GraphEQA (graph EQA). Smoke tests in `src/test/memory/test_memory_backends_smoke.py`. See `docs/plans/TESTING_BACKENDS.md`.
- When changing behavior, run the relevant tests and fix any failures before committing. Prefer invoking tests via **`emet test`** so the project env (uv) is used.

## Git (agent behavior)
- **NEVER push to `main` or `master`.** Do not `git push origin main`, do not merge a feature branch into `main` and push. Shared `main` is updated via PR on GitHub, not agent direct push.
- **To bring in latest `main`:** stay on the feature branch, `git fetch origin`, `git merge origin/main`, fix conflicts, commit, then `git push origin <feature-branch>` only.
- If the user says “merge main”, they mean **merge `main` into the current feature branch**, not the reverse—unless they explicitly say to land changes on `main` via a PR they will merge themselves.

## Unified config
- Default nested YAML: **`configs/emet/default.yaml`**. Override with **`--config`** / **`-C`** or env **`EMET_CONFIG`**. Dot overrides: **`--set mapping.depth_source=auto`**, **`-O agent.eqa=true`**.
- Legacy flat files (`dynav_config.yaml`, `dynav_innate_mars.yaml`) still load; `dynav_innate_mars.yaml` is a thin **`extends:`** stub — innate_mars tuning lives under **`robots.innate_mars`** in the default config. See **`docs/emet_config.md`** and **`docs/AGENT_RUN.md`**.
- **`get_parameters("dynav_innate_mars.yaml")`** must resolve robot overlay (e.g. `depth_source=auto`, `graph_object_fusion.bounds_3d_iou_merge_min=0.40`). Smoke: `uv run emet test src/test/config/`.

## GPU / eval workflow (agent behavior)
- **One GPU-heavy job at a time** on the workstation GPU (often shared with Xorg/gnome-shell). Before Habitat HM-EQA, SQA3D real sweeps, Robocasa explore, or dynagraph with VLM: run **`uv run emet eval status`**, **`uv run emet eval diagnose`**, then **`uv run emet eval kill-stale`** only if nothing intentional is live, then **`NEED_MIB=12000 uv run emet eval wait`** (or **`emet eval check`**). Bash: `./scripts/gpu_preflight.sh` still works (delegates to `emet eval`). Prefer **`emet eval`** over raw `pkill` / ad-hoc process kills.
- **Empty `nvidia-smi` ≠ safe for Habitat.** Free VRAM does not prove Magnum EGL works. HM-EQA can fail with `unable to find CUDA device 0 among N EGL devices` / `WindowlessContext` while the GPU looks idle. Cursor agent “crashes” here are usually **`emet` segfaults** (null IP / invalid opcode) from Habitat/VLM teardown in the agent tool tree — not a hidden CUDA process. See **`docs/known_issues.md`** and **`.cursor/rules/gpu-eval-workflow.mdc`**.
- **Do not chain** Robocasa dynagraph smoke → full pytest (MuJoCo-native paths) → Habitat VLM eval in one session — that pattern caused NVIDIA driver hangs (GUI + SSH dead). Cross-track smoke defaults **`RUN_DEEP_EVAL=0`**; run **`run_overnight_eval_smoke.sh`** on a **separate night**. See **`docs/evaluation.md`** and **`docs/experiments/cross_track_smoke.md`**.
- **Long Habitat / overnight evals:** launch via **`uv run emet jobs run --name … -- CMD`** (not bare `nohup` when avoidable). Examples: overnight battery, cross-track smoke, HM-EQA H2H. Do **not** run Habitat/VLM as blocking inline Cursor agent commands, and do **not** hard-kill mid-episode Habitat smokes from the agent (use **`emet jobs cancel`**). After agent death: **`bash scripts/status_log.sh tail`** from the owning checkout, then **`emet jobs`**, **`~/runs/emet/`**, **`~/.cache/habitat_eqa/results/`**. Do not `tail ~/runs/emet/STATUS.log` (shared across sibling trees).
- **Record before risky sim/GPU work:** assume the Cursor session will die. Before Habitat/MuJoCo/VLM launches, resumes, `kill-stale`, or affinity experiments, leave a tail-able **`next:`** via **`scripts/status_log.sh`** (per-repo under **`~/runs/emet/status/<repo>/`**) and update **`segfault.md`** / the active investigation note with job id, OUT, commit, and the exact resume command. See **`.cursor/rules/gpu-eval-workflow.mdc`**.
- **Paper simulation battery:** seven sequential tracks — **`docs/simulation_testing_plan.md`**, **`./scripts/run_simulation_smoke_battery.sh`** (Habitat EQA → Habitat OVMM → Robocasa search → Molmo search → SQA3D → Robocasa dynamic env → Molmo dynamic search).
- Full **`pytest -m "not sim"`** must pass **`emet_pytest_no_sim_ignore_args`** from **`scripts/gpu_preflight.sh`** (excludes unmarked MuJoCo/Habitat sim tests under `src/test/simulation/`, etc.).
- **Orphans / hung evals:** new sim/eval `Popen` must use **`emet.utils.process_tree`**; after hangs run **`emet eval status`** before re-launch. Do not call **`emet eval kill-stale`** from inside a smoke that must stay alive (use **`wait`** only). Details: **`.cursor/rules/gpu-eval-workflow.mdc`**, **`docs/known_issues.md`**.
- **Job registry (required for long GPU runs):** use **`uv run emet jobs run --name … [--need-mib N] -- CMD`**. Monitor with **`emet jobs`** / **`emet jobs status JOB_ID`** (progress + ETA), **`emet jobs logs`**, **`emet jobs cancel`**. Registry: **`~/runs/emet/jobs/`**. Scripts that heartbeats should honor **`EMET_JOB_ID`** and call **`emet jobs update … --units-done/--units-total/--phase/--current-id`** (and/or write **`OUT/progress.json`**). Do not start paper/HM-EQA/overnight jobs with unmanaged bare `nohup` unless adopting them with **`emet jobs register`** afterward.

## User-facing commands (agent behavior)
- **Before suggesting shell commands** to the user, **run them yourself** when the workspace and environment allow (from repo root: `uv run emet …`, `uv run python …`, smoke `timeout … emet serve …`, etc.). Confirm paths, flags, and typical stderr; then report what actually happened instead of only pasting commands for the user to discover errors.
- **Before sending code that wires config → constructors** (e.g. `build_rerun_visualizer_kwargs` → `RerunVisualizer`), run a smoke import/instantiate or a unit test that asserts kwargs match `inspect.signature(...)`; do not rely on pytest alone if you did not run it.
- **Verify CLI flags before every suggested command** (do not guess from memory or from other subcommands):
  - Run **`uv run python -m emet.app.<module> --help`** for the specific app (e.g. `run_dynagraph`, `run_dynamem`, `run_agent`) or **`uv run emet run <subcommand> --help`** when the top-level group exposes it.
  - For GPU preflight: **`uv run emet eval --help`** / **`status`** before suggesting `kill-stale` / `wait` / `check`.
  - If a flag might be missing from the wrapper help, check the app module’s Click options in `src/emet/app/`.
  - Never tell the user to pass a flag until `--help` lists it (or you just added it in the same change).
- **Rerun world frame**: Log map/voxels/graph under `world/…` in navigation world coordinates. Live `Spatial3DView` blueprint must use **`origin="world"`** (not `world/robot`) or the map appears to rotate with the base. See `docs/rerun.md` and `spatial3d_view_world()` in `src/emet/visualization/rerun.py`.
- **Rerun flags differ by subcommand** (common mistake: `--rerun` on dynagraph/dynamem):
  - **`emet run agent`**: Rerun **off** by default → pass **`--rerun`** to enable.
  - **`emet run dynamem`**, **`emet run dynagraph`**, **`emet run scene-graph`**: Rerun **on** by default → omit flags, or **`--no-rerun`** to disable. Do **not** use **`--rerun`** unless `--help` shows it (compatibility alias may exist).
  - Shared when Rerun is enabled: **`--headless`**, **`--rerun-native`**, **`--rerun-show-panels`**, **`--rerun-debug`**, **`--rerun-bind`**; dynagraph/dynamem also **`--save_rerun` / `--SR`**.
- **Before claiming a sim / spawn / placement bug is fixed**, run a **concrete verification experiment** in this repo and **compare numbers in the output** (do not hand-wave). Examples: `timeout … uv run python -m emet.simulation.mujoco_server --robot innate_mars --use-robocasa --headless --seed 0` and confirm **scene summary** `Robot position (x, y, theta)` matches the **Robocasa planar autoplace** log line (`moved base to x=… y=…`) within a few millimeters; or a small `uv run python …` script that loads the merged MJCF and asserts bounds. Paste or summarize the measured outcome. Do not treat “tests passed” or code review alone as proof for behavior-only regressions. **Avoid** calling `mj_fwdPosition` alone after `mj_forward` + actuator sync on planar Robocasa merges; it can desync `body_xpos` from `qpos` for this stack—extend with a full `mj_forward` only when you know the model needs it, or skip the extra forward if `write_planar_base_xyt` already forwarded.

## Dependencies
- **rerun-sdk**: Use `>=0.21.0,<0.23.0` (compatible with lerobot). Do not pin to 0.18.x.
- **pinocchio / hppfcl**: The dynamics library is installed as the **pin** package (PyPI). Pinocchio imports the **hppfcl** module at load time when built with collision support. Always list **hpp-fcl** in `pyproject.toml` dependencies so `uv sync` (or `pip install -e .`) installs it; otherwise `emet serve mujoco --robot stretch` fails with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'hppfcl'`. **Do not** fix dependency or import issues by editing or patching anything under **.venv**; fix only via `pyproject.toml` (add/version deps) and re-run `uv sync`.
- **third_party/robocasa**: This repo uses a fork. Keep `lerobot==0.3.3` and `mujoco>=3.4.0` in `install_requires` in `third_party/robocasa/setup.py`. Keep `mujoco>=3.4.0` in pyproject.toml `[tool.uv]` override-dependencies so the resolver uses the local robocasa (PyPI robocasa pins mujoco==3.2.6 and would otherwise be selected when the path is not considered).
- **pyproject.toml** and **src/setup.py**: Keep dependency versions in sync where both exist.
- **third_party/robosuite**: Keep `mujoco` requirement aligned with `pyproject.toml` sim extra (e.g. `mujoco>=3.4.0`). Robocasa imports `get_elements` from robosuite's `mjcf_utils`; use the local fork so that API is available.

## Package layout
- Main package is `emet` under `src/`. CLI entrypoint: `emet` (see `emet.cli:main`).
- Apps and visualization: `src/emet/app/`, `src/emet/visualization/` (e.g. rerun in `src/emet/visualization/rerun.py`).
- Rerun usage appears in dynamem, mapping, and logging; keep usage compatible with rerun-sdk 0.21+.

## Code quality
- Use **ruff** for linting (see `[tool.ruff]` in pyproject.toml). Pre-commit is enabled for this repo.
- Prefer project style (ruff/black/isort as configured); avoid ad-hoc formatting.
- **Imports**: Place all imports at the top of the file. Use inline imports only when necessary (e.g. to avoid circular imports or to defer loading a heavy optional dependency).
- **Avoid unnecessary defensiveness**: Prefer fixing `pyproject.toml` (dependencies, extras) over try/except for missing imports or optional features. Use try/except only when there is a real runtime contingency, not to paper over missing declared deps.
- **Before committing** (see also `.cursor/rules/branch-consistency.mdc`):
  1. Run `git diff origin/main HEAD --stat` and skim the full diff for behavior changes.
  2. **Code ↔ docs:** every new/changed module under `src/emet/simulation/` or `src/emet/app/`, or new CLI subcommand, must appear in the right doc (`docs/cli.md`, topic doc, or `docs/simulation_modules.md`).
  3. **CLI ↔ docs:** compare `emet <cmd> --help` against `docs/cli.md` and topic docs; defaults must match `resolve_serve_robot()` / dataclass defaults.
  4. **Env vars:** new `EMET_*` toggles in changed Python must be listed in `docs/environment_variables.md` or a topic env doc (e.g. `docs/molmospaces_environment_variables.md`).
  5. **Defaults alignment:** core `emet` CLI, `packages/emet_molmospaces/emet_molmospaces/runner.py`, and these rules must agree (MolmoSpaces default robot: **stretch**).
  6. **Tests:** add/update CLI help tests when adding subcommands.
  7. Trim "AI slop"—unnecessary try/except, vague comments, over-defensive checks. Prefer clear failures and declared deps over silent fallbacks.

## Simulation
- Default `./install.sh` profile is **full** (sim on when `third_party/robocasa` exists; use `--no-sim` or `--profile=minimal` for lightweight/CI). MolmoSpaces wrapper venv is still created when `packages/emet_molmospaces` exists unless `--no-molmospaces`.
- MuJoCo sim: `emet serve mujoco --use-robocasa` (or `emet serve robocasa`). Sim is **present** when `third_party/robocasa` and `third_party/robosuite` exist; `emet sync --all` then includes the sim extra.
- DynaMem: `emet run dynamem ...`. Rerun viewer: `http://localhost:9090?url=ws://localhost:9877`.
- Simulation install: `./install.sh -y` (default includes sim when third_party is present); or `./install.sh --sim -y`; robocasa/robosuite come from `third_party/` (see install scripts). Robocasa kitchen assets must include **fixtures_lw** (LightWheel registry) for `emet serve robocasa` — `scripts/download_robocasa_assets.py` fetches it automatically.

## MolmoSpaces (optional wrapper)
- **Install**: `./install.sh -y` (with default sim) also creates `.venv-molmospaces` when `packages/emet_molmospaces` exists; use `--no-molmospaces` to skip. Wrapper-only: `./install.sh --molmospaces -y`. Core emet delegates `merge-scene` / `list-scenes` to that wrapper (molmo-spaces needs mujoco 3.4 + numpy≥2.2, separate from main `.venv`).
- **Usage**: `emet serve molmospaces --molmospaces-index 0 --headless` (or `emet serve mujoco --molmospaces-scene ithor …`) merges scene+robot then starts the ZMQ server; default robot is **stretch** when `--robot` is omitted. Use `--robot rby1` for Galaxea R1. `emet serve robocasa` is the Robocasa shortcut. `ensure_molmospaces_assets_dir_env()` sets default `MLSPACES_ASSETS_DIR` / `MLSPACES_CACHE_DIR` (sibling dirs under `~/.cache/molmospaces/`) if unset—do not point both at the same path.
- **Testing after MolmoSpaces changes**: Run `uv run emet test src/test/cli/test_molmospaces_cli.py` (and `-- -q` if passing pytest flags). Optional integration: `RUN_MOLMOSPACES_TESTS=1 uv run emet test src/test/cli/test_molmospaces_cli.py -k ...` when `.venv-molmospaces` is installed. Wrapper unit tests: `uv run pytest packages/emet_molmospaces/tests/ -q`. Smoke: short `timeout 60 uv run emet serve mujoco --molmospaces-scene ithor --molmospaces-split train --molmospaces-index 0 --headless` should reach “Server running” without MJCF load errors (default stretch; add `--robot rby1` to smoke Galaxea).
- **Code touchpoints**: `src/emet/simulation/molmospaces_config.py` (defaults, `ensure_molmo_asset_layout_symlinks`, `galaxea_r1_assets_directory`), `src/emet/simulation/molmospaces_env.py` (`EMET_MOLMOSPACES_NAV_TELEPORT`, etc.), `src/emet/cli.py` (`--molmospaces-*`), `src/emet/simulation/mujoco_server.py` (load + symlink prep), `packages/emet_molmospaces/emet_molmospaces/runner.py` (merge, resource cache). Details: `docs/molmospaces.md`; env vars: `docs/molmospaces_environment_variables.md`.
